{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally Gets a Job at a Magazine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I'll Do My Best", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (you use the modal <span class=\"strong\">will</span> in the Future tense) to talk about actions you are going to do in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).<br/><br><span class=\"italic\">Example: If I don't work for a magazine, I might work for another kind of publication;  I may apply to a PR firm if I see an opportunity.</span><br><br> You can use the first conditional to talk about possible actions and situations in the future.<br/><br/>  There are two parts to the sentence. <br/><br/>  One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>.<br/><br/>   Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If*</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/won't</span><br/> You use a comma after the condition in this form. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: If I work for a newspaper, I will learn a lot.</span><br><br> * You can use other words instead of <span class=\"italic\">if</span>, you can use <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span> or <span class=\"italic\">when</span>.<br/><br/>  You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Before you apply</span>,<br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">After graduation</span>,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you may want to research the company.</span><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">we will open up a business.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I will work for a magazine</span>,<br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I will apply for a job</span>,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">after I finish school.</span><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">if I see one of interest.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "editor-in-chief", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the person who is in charge of a group of editors (the editorial team)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you meet the editor-in-chief  during your meet and greet?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "magazine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large thin book that contains news stories, articles and photographs ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Will you always work for a magazine?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Opinions and Asking for Clarification ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk to people, you can use different expressions for different things:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you don't understand what a person is saying, you can ask for clarification.<br/> If you want to share your opinion, you can introduce it with an expression.<br/> Here are some expressions you can use:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Expressing an Opinion\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Asking for Clarification\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">(Personally,) I think \u2026</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">In my opinion \u2026</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would like to point out \u2026 </span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The way I see it \u2026</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'd say that \u2026 </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What did you say?</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you repeat what you said, please?</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you talking \u2026 ?</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you be more specific please?</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you explain what you mean?</span><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">What do you mean by that?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "publication", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a magazine, paper, etc., that is printed and made available to the public ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I might work for another kind of publication like a newspaper.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to come in handy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that will be useful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Doing research before you interview may come in handy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "start", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the beginning of someone's job, which they will develop in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This will be a great start to your career.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose one of the options: <ul><li>You are going to work for a magazine. Will you do it?</li><li>You are going to write an article for the newspaper. Will you do it?</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Which one would you choose? Write down 3-4 sentences explaining why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the possible events and actions that may happen in the future because of your choice. Use words like <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> in your sentences. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I tell a friend about possible events in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about jobs and work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about actions related to work.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs and work. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarifications and introduce an opinion.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content":